<p>HUB International is the <strong>sixth-largest insurance broker in the world</strong> by revenue, the <strong>largest privately held insurance broker by valuation</strong>, and one of the two most acquisitive brokers in any given year. Headquartered in Chicago. Founded in 1998 through the merger of 11 Canadian brokerages. Owned by a stack of private-equity sponsors since 2007, currently led by <strong>Hellman &amp; Friedman</strong> (since 2013) with <strong>Altas Partners</strong> (2018) and <strong>Leonard Green &amp; Partners</strong> (2023) as minority partners. A May 2025 capital raise added <strong>T. Rowe Price, Alpha Wave Global, and Temasek</strong> at a $29B valuation — a deliberately public-market-friendly investor base, ahead of an IPO targeted for late 2026 or early 2027.</p>
<p>Revenue trajectory tells the story: <strong>$1.1B in 2013 → $2B+ in 2018 → $3.7B in 2023 → $4.77B in 2024</strong>. Organic growth was 7.3% in 2024 — the rest came from the M&amp;A engine. Roughly 19,000 employees across 570+ offices in the U.S. and Canada.</p>
"""),
    ("The ownership ladder",
