</ul>
"""),
    ("The seven big risks",
     "What could break the thesis",
     """
<ol>
<li><strong>Integration drag.</strong> 600+ acquired firms with different cultures, systems, contracts, and producer compensation structures. If integration falters, organic growth slows and the multiple collapses. <em>This is the area where ERP Unite is most directly relevant as a solution.</em></li>
<li><strong>Fee compression.</strong> RPA fees have been declining for a decade as plan sponsors get smarter about benchmarking. If average fees compress faster than HUB can add services, margins erode.</li>
<li><strong>Recordkeeper consolidation.</strong> Top 5 recordkeepers hold ~60%+ of assets. They gain leverage and could try to bypass advisors and serve plans directly.</li>
<li><strong>ERISA litigation against advisors.</strong> Plaintiffs increasingly name RPAs as defendants. A bad fee-case loss against HUB or a peer would reshape industry economics.</li>
<li><strong>PE exit pressure.</strong> H&amp;F has held 13 years. At some point an exit is forced. IPO is the plan; if 2027 markets are bad, secondary buyouts or strategic sales become harder.</li>
<li><strong>Recession / market drop.</strong> RPA revenue is asset-based — a 25% market correction immediately compresses revenue by 20%+ industry-wide.</li>
<li><strong>Talent retention.</strong> Producers have equity in their books. If HUB's culture or comp model alienates them, they walk to competitors. Harder to manage at scale.</li>
</ol>
"""),
    ("The 24-month view",
     "Mid-2026 to mid-2028",
     """
<ul>
