"05-regulatory": [
    ("cover", None, """
# Regulatory
## **foundations**

ERISA. SECURE Acts. The DOL Fiduciary Rule saga. And the litigation pressure that drives the entire business.

<div class="byline">Module 05 · why audit trails are the product, not a feature</div>
"""),
    ("stat", None, """
<div class="number">1974</div>

## ERISA — the foundation under everything

Passed in response to corporate pension failures in the 1960s. Every fiduciary role, fee disclosure, and prohibited transaction in RPW exists inside this law.
"""),
    ("", "ERISA — the concepts you actually need", """
- **Fiduciary duty** — Loyalty (act solely in participants' interest) + Prudence (care of a *prudent expert*)
- **§3(16)** — Plan Administrator (admin role; usually a TPA)
- **§3(21)** — Investment Advice Fiduciary (advisor recommends; sponsor decides)
- **§3(38)** — Investment Manager (discretionary; advisor takes the liability)
- **§408(b)(2)** — Service provider fee disclosure
- **§404(c)** — Participant-directed investment protection
- **§406** — Prohibited transactions (self-dealing, related-party)
- **Form 5500** — Annual filing to DOL/IRS; 100+ participants requires audit

*Net: every RPW contract specifies a fiduciary role. The 408(b)(2) disclosure is how plan sponsors meet their compliance obligation.*
"""),
    ("section section-color-2", None, """
# SECURE Act (2019)

First major retirement reform in a decade.
"""),
    ("", "Key provisions of SECURE 1.0", """
- **Pooled Employer Plans (PEPs)** — unrelated employers can join a single 401(k) sponsored by a **Pooled Plan Provider (PPP)**
- **Multiple Employer Plans (MEPs)** rules clarified
- **RMD age** raised from 70½ to 72
- **Long-term part-time coverage** — 3 consecutive years + 500+ hours
- **Lifetime income disclosures** on participant statements
- **Annuity safe harbor** for DC plans

*Net: PEPs made 401(k) plans economically viable for very small employers. The "One Bad Apple" rule was removed — one bad employer no longer disqualifies the whole MEP.*
"""),
    ("section section-color-3", None, """
# SECURE 2.0 (Dec 2022)

The more important one. 90+ provisions. Phased 2023–2027.
"""),
    ("", "The phased rollout — what's already live", """
<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **2023** — RMD age to 73
Startup tax credit: 50% → **100% of costs** (≤50 employees). New $1,000/employee credit for employer contributions. 403(b) can join PEPs/MEPs.

### **2024**
Pension-Linked Emergency Savings ($2,500 in-plan). **Student loan matching.** Roth employer matching allowed.

</div>
<div class="card">

### **Jan 1, 2025** — the big one
**Mandatory auto-enrollment** for new 401(k) and 403(b) plans. 3% default, escalating 1%/year to 10–15%. Existing plans grandfathered.

### **Starter 401(k)** plans for first-time sponsors.

</div>
</div>
"""),
    ("", "What's coming — and the consulting-revenue waves", """
<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **2026** — Roth catch-up requirement
High earners (>$145K) must put age-50+ catch-up contributions in **Roth** (after-tax). Originally 2024, delayed because recordkeepers weren't ready.

**Forces recordkeeper upgrades across HUB's entire book = RFP wave for HUB RPW.**

</div>
<div class="card">

### **Dec 31, 2026** — amendment deadline
Most plans must be **amended for SECURE 2.0 by year-end 2026**.

**This creates billable consulting work right now** across every HUB plan-sponsor client.

### **2027** — Saver's Match
Federal match for low-income workers replaces Saver's Credit.

</div>
</div>
"""),
    ("section", None, """
# The DOL Fiduciary Rule saga

Still unresolved in 2026. Rollover advice is the regulatory hot zone.
"""),
    ("", "The four-decade tug-of-war", """
- **1975 DOL Rule** — five-part test. Advisors structured around it.
- **2016 Obama Rule** — expanded fiduciary. ⛔ Vacated by 5th Circuit 2018.
- **2020 Trump Rule** — **PTE 2020-02**. Still in effect.
- **2024 Biden "Retirement Security Rule"** — expanded fiduciary again. ⛔ Partially blocked late 2024.
- **2025–26** — DOL signaled it won't defend the 2024 rule. **PTE 2020-02 is operative.**

*Net: when HUB advises a participant to roll over to a HUB-managed IRA, every step must comply with **PTE 2020-02 Impartial Conduct Standards** — documented, defensible, audit-trail-able. Every rollover.*
"""),
    ("", "ERISA litigation — the threat that drives demand", """
- **Tussey v. ABB (2007)** started the modern wave
- **Tibble v. Edison (2015)** went to SCOTUS — established **ongoing duty to monitor investments**
- **200+ class-action filings per year** by the early 2020s
- Plaintiffs increasingly name **the advisor** as co-defendant on 3(38) cases

*Net: sponsors hire RPAs specifically to (a) reduce litigation risk through documented fiduciary process, (b) shift risk via 3(38) delegation, (c) get expert witnesses ready. **The audit trail isn't a nice-to-have — it's the product.***
"""),
    ("", "HSO implication", """
<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### Documented decision lineage is regulatory output
If we touch RPW data, every fund replacement, fee change, recommendation needs a defensible **"who decided, on what evidence, on what date"** chain. AH journal four-eye + authorization framework are the right primitives.

</div>
<div class="card">

### The Roth catch-up requirement is a near-term wedge
Every plan with high earners has to comply in 2026. **Forces recordkeeper conversations across HUB's entire book.** Position ERP Unite as the system that ingests post-Roth-conversion feeds cleanly.

</div>
</div>
"""),
],

