"""),
    ("section section-color-2", None, """
# IPO path

Late 2026 / early 2027. SOX prep already in flight.
"""),
    ("", "What an IPO unlocks for HUB", """
- **Currency for larger acquisitions** — stock-based deals against publicly traded peers
- **Liquidity** for employees (~30% own equity) + PE sponsors (gradual exit)
- **Higher multiple** — public scarcity premium pushes likely IPO above $30B
- **Cohen has said operational readiness target is late 2026 / early 2027** — S-1 timing depends on market

*Net: the next 12–18 months at HUB are dominated by IPO prep workstreams — SOX, audit, legal, regulatory, investor relations.*
"""),
    ("section section-color-1", None, """
# Seven real risks

What could break the thesis.
"""),
    ("", "Risks 1–4 — the operational ones", """
1. **Integration drag** · 600+ acquired firms, different cultures, systems, comp structures. *This is where ERP Unite is most directly the solution.*
2. **Fee compression** · RPA fees have been declining for a decade. If they compress faster than services grow, margins erode.
3. **Recordkeeper consolidation** · Top 5 hold ~60%+. They could try to bypass advisors and serve sponsors directly.
4. **ERISA litigation against advisors** · Plaintiffs naming RPAs as co-defendants is rising. A bad fee-case loss against a major aggregator would reshape industry economics.
"""),
    ("", "Risks 5–7 — the financial ones", """
5. **PE exit pressure** · H&F has held 13 years. An exit is eventually forced. IPO is the plan; if 2027 markets are bad, alternatives are harder.
6. **Recession / market drop** · RPA revenue is asset-based. **A 25% market correction immediately compresses revenue by 20%+** industry-wide.
7. **Talent retention** · Producers have equity in their books. If HUB's culture or comp model alienates them, they walk. Harder to manage at scale.
"""),
    ("section section-color-3", None, """
# 24-month view

Mid-2026 to mid-2028.
"""),
    ("", "What to expect, year by year", """
- **2026** · SECURE 2.0 amendment deadline drives consulting. 50–70 more acquisitions. IPO prep visible in disclosures.
- **Late 2026 / early 2027** · S-1 filing if conditions favorable. IPO targets $30B+.
- **2027** · If public, first earnings cycles. Pressure to show organic growth. **M&A may slow** as integration becomes the public-market narrative.
- **2027–28** · Possible large-scale acquisition once stock currency is available. Capture of a sizable RPA aggregator or EB-focused competitor.

*Net: HUB will spend the next 2 years simultaneously buying companies, integrating them, and preparing financial reporting for public-market scrutiny. **Three things ERP Unite is built for.***
"""),
    ("section section-color-4", None, """
# The deal posture

What this all points to for HSO's first conversation.
"""),
    ("", "Engagement posture summary", """
<div class="cols two">
<div class="card">

### **1. Lead with integration**
HUB's #1 named risk is integration drag. ERP Unite is literally a solution. **Position it that way, not as "a better commission system."**

### **2. Audit-trail every conversation**
Pre-IPO finance orgs care about SOX, defensible documentation, reproducibility. **Every demo foregrounds these capabilities.**

</div>
<div class="card">

### **3. RPW is the deal-defining question**
In scope = multi-year HSO product investment for AUM-billing extensions. Out of scope = focused P&C + EB engagement with IntegrationHub as the seam. **Decide before discovery, don't drift.**

### **4. Mid-Atlantic is the easy first foothold**
AFS (Bethesda, MD) + WFG (McLean, VA) is geographically nearby, well-led. **If a pilot region is on the table, this is it.**

</div>
</div>
"""),
],
}


# ─── Marp deck renderer ───────────────────────────────────────────────────

def render_deck(idx: int) -> str:
    """Render module idx as a Marp markdown deck."""
    m = MODULES[idx]
    slides = DECKS[m["slug"]]

    title_clean = f"{m['title_word']} {m['title_emph']}".strip()
    frontmatter = f"""---
marp: true
theme: hso-knowledge
paginate: true
size: 16:9
title: HUB International primer — Module {m['num']} · {title_clean}
---
"""

    rendered_slides = []
    for slide_class, header, body in slides:
        parts = []
        if slide_class:
            parts.append(f"<!-- _class: {slide_class} -->")
        if header:
            parts.append(f"# {header}")
        parts.append(body.strip())
        rendered_slides.append("\n\n".join(parts))

    return frontmatter + "\n\n---\n\n".join(rendered_slides) + "\n"


# ─── Shared CSS (single source of truth, embedded per page) ───────────────
STYLE = """
:root { --navy: #00395F; --navy-dark: #00253D; --navy-light: #1A5A8A; --cyan: #079FC3; --cyan-light: #4AB9D4; --teal: #00B294; --red: #F1554B; --yellow: #F2B949; --slate: #44546A; --mute: #737373; --bg: #FAFBFC; --border: #E5E9EE; }
* { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }
html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }
body { font-family: 'Segoe UI', sans-serif; color: var(--navy); background: var(--bg); line-height: 1.6; }

.hub-hero { background: linear-gradient(135deg, var(--navy-dark) 0%, var(--navy) 50%, var(--navy-light) 100%); color: white; padding: 64px 40px 84px; position: relative; overflow: hidden; }
.hub-hero::before { content: ''; position: absolute; top: -50%; right: -10%; width: 600px; height: 600px; background: radial-gradient(circle, rgba(7, 159, 195, 0.22) 0%, transparent 65%); pointer-events: none; }
.hub-hero::after { content: ''; position: absolute; bottom: 0; left: 0; right: 0; height: 4px; background: linear-gradient(90deg, var(--cyan) 0%, var(--teal) 50%, var(--cyan) 100%); }
.hub-hero-inner { max-width: 1200px; margin: 0 auto; position: relative; }
.breadcrumb { color: var(--cyan-light); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.breadcrumb a { color: var(--cyan-light); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(74, 185, 212, 0.5); padding-bottom: 2px; }
.breadcrumb a:hover { border-color: var(--cyan-light); }
.breadcrumb .sep { opacity: 0.5; margin: 0 8px; }
.module-num { display: inline-block; background: rgba(7, 159, 195, 0.18); border: 1px solid var(--cyan); color: var(--cyan-light); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; padding: 5px 12px; border-radius: 18px; margin-bottom: 14px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.hub-hero h1 { font-size: 60px; font-weight: 300; letter-spacing: -1.5px; line-height: 1.04; margin-bottom: 16px; }
.hub-hero h1 strong { font-weight: 600; color: var(--cyan-light); }
.hub-hero .tagline { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 300; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); max-width: 880px; margin-bottom: 36px; }
.hub-stats { display: flex; gap: 48px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 12px; }
.hub-stat { border-left: 3px solid var(--cyan); padding-left: 16px; }
.hub-stat-value { font-size: 26px; font-weight: 600; color: white; line-height: 1; }
.hub-stat-label { font-size: 13px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); margin-top: 6px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; }

main { max-width: 1100px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 56px 40px 80px; }
.section { background: white; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 14px; padding: 36px 44px; margin-bottom: 28px; box-shadow: 0 6px 18px rgba(0,57,95,0.05); }
.section-eyebrow { color: var(--cyan); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 2px; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 12px; }
.section h2 { font-size: 28px; font-weight: 500; color: var(--navy); margin-bottom: 18px; }
.section p, .section li { font-size: 16.5px; color: #1F2D3D; line-height: 1.72; }
.section p { margin-bottom: 14px; }
.section ul, .section ol { padding-left: 26px; margin-bottom: 14px; }
.section ul li, .section ol li { margin-bottom: 6px; }
.section ul ul, .section ol ol { margin-top: 6px; margin-bottom: 6px; }
.section strong { color: var(--navy); font-weight: 600; }
.section em { color: var(--slate); }
.section code { background: #F4F7FA; color: var(--navy); padding: 1px 6px; border-radius: 4px; font-family: 'Cascadia Code', 'Consolas', monospace; font-size: 0.92em; border: 1px solid #DCE3EB; }
.section a { color: var(--cyan); border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(7, 159, 195, 0.5); text-decoration: none; padding-bottom: 1px; }
.section a:hover { color: var(--navy-dark); border-color: var(--navy-dark); }

.section table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 14px 0 18px 0; font-size: 15px; }
.section table th { background: var(--navy); color: white; text-align: left; padding: 10px 14px; font-weight: 600; font-size: 13.5px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; text-transform: uppercase; }
.section table td { padding: 12px 14px; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); color: #1F2D3D; vertical-align: top; }
.section table tr:nth-child(even) td { background: #F8FAFC; }
.section table tr:last-child td { border-bottom: none; }

.callout { background: linear-gradient(135deg, #F4FAFD 0%, #FAFCFD 100%); border: 1px solid #C3DCEA; border-left: 4px solid var(--cyan); border-radius: 10px; padding: 22px 28px; margin: 18px 0 6px 0; }
.callout-eyebrow { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; letter-spacing: 1.5px; color: var(--cyan); text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.callout p { font-size: 15.5px; line-height: 1.7; }
.callout ul, .callout ol { padding-left: 22px; }
.callout-flow p { padding-left: 0; margin-bottom: 10px; }
.callout-split { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 28px; }
@media (max-width: 720px) { .callout-split { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }

.test-yourself { padding-left: 22px; }
.test-yourself li { margin-bottom: 10px; }

.hub-nav { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr auto 1fr; gap: 12px; align-items: stretch; margin: 48px 0 0 0; }
.hub-nav-btn { background: white; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 14px 20px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--navy); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 4px; transition: border-color 0.15s ease, background 0.15s ease, transform 0.15s ease; min-width: 0; }
.hub-nav-btn:hover:not(.disabled) { border-color: var(--cyan); background: #F0F6FB; transform: translateY(-1px); }
.hub-nav-btn.next { text-align: right; }
.hub-nav-btn.disabled { opacity: 0.45; cursor: default; }
.hub-nav-label { font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 1px; color: var(--cyan); }
.hub-nav-btn.disabled .hub-nav-label { color: var(--mute); }
.hub-nav-title { font-size: 15px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
.hub-nav-pos { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: center; justify-content: center; background: white; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 24px; text-decoration: none; color: var(--slate); font-size: 12px; letter-spacing: 0.5px; white-space: nowrap; }
.hub-nav-pos:hover { border-color: var(--cyan); color: var(--cyan); }

.deck-link { margin-top: 28px; display: inline-flex; flex-wrap: wrap; align-items: center; gap: 10px; }
.deck-link .deck-btn { color: white; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 600; font-size: 14px; padding: 9px 18px; border-radius: 8px; background: var(--cyan); border: 1px solid var(--cyan); transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease; }
.deck-link .deck-btn:hover { background: var(--cyan-light); border-color: var(--cyan-light); color: var(--navy-dark); }
.deck-link .deck-btn-secondary { background: transparent; border-color: rgba(255,255,255,0.4); }
.deck-link .deck-btn-secondary:hover { background: white; color: var(--navy); border-color: white; }
.deck-link .deck-btn-watch { background: var(--teal); border-color: var(--teal); }
.deck-link .deck-btn-watch:hover { background: var(--cyan); border-color: var(--cyan); color: white; }
.deck-link .deck-meta { font-size: 12px; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.65); letter-spacing: 0.5px; margin-left: 6px; }

footer { background: var(--navy-dark); color: rgba(255,255,255,0.7); padding: 24px 40px; text-align: center; font-size: 13px; }
footer a { color: var(--cyan-light); text-decoration: none; border-bottom: 1px dotted rgba(74, 185, 212, 0.5); }
footer a:hover { color: white; border-color: white; }

@media (max-width: 720px) { .hub-hero h1 { font-size: 40px; } .hub-hero .tagline { font-size: 17px; } .hub-nav { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } main { padding: 32px 20px; } .section { padding: 24px 22px; } }
""".strip()


VIDEO_MODAL_SNIPPET = """
<!-- ───────────── Video modal — resizable, theatre-mode, native ESC ───────────── -->
<dialog id="video-modal" aria-label="Narrated deck player">
  <div class="video-frame">
    <button class="video-action video-close" type="button" aria-label="Close video" title="Close (Esc)">×</button>
    <button class="video-action video-max"   type="button" aria-label="Toggle theatre"  title="Theatre / restore (F)">⛶</button>
    <video class="video-player" controls preload="metadata" playsinline></video>
    <div class="video-title"></div>
  </div>
</dialog>
<style>
  #video-modal { background: transparent; border: none; padding: 0; position: fixed; inset: 0; margin: auto; width: max-content; height: max-content; max-width: 100vw; max-height: 100vh; overflow: visible; color: white; }
  #video-modal::backdrop { background: rgba(0, 37, 61, 0.82); backdrop-filter: blur(6px); }
  #video-modal .video-frame { position: relative; background: #000; border-radius: 12px; box-shadow: 0 30px 80px rgba(0,0,0,0.65); width: clamp(320px, 90vw, 1600px); resize: both; overflow: hidden; min-width: 320px; min-height: 240px; max-width: 96vw; max-height: 92vh; }
  #video-modal.maximized .video-frame { width: 96vw !important; height: 92vh !important; max-width: 96vw; max-height: 92vh; resize: none; border-radius: 8px; }
  #video-modal .video-player { display: block; width: 100%; height: calc(100% - 48px); background: #000; }
  #video-modal .video-title { height: 48px; padding: 12px 22px; font-size: 14px; font-weight: 500; color: rgba(255,255,255,0.85); border-top: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.1); background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(0,0,0,0) 0%, rgba(0,37,61,0.6) 100%); box-sizing: border-box; white-space: nowrap; overflow: hidden; text-overflow: ellipsis; }
  #video-modal .video-action { position: absolute; top: 12px; width: 36px; height: 36px; border-radius: 50%; background: rgba(0, 37, 61, 0.7); backdrop-filter: blur(4px); color: white; border: 1px solid rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.2); font-size: 18px; line-height: 1; cursor: pointer; z-index: 2; transition: background 0.15s ease, transform 0.15s ease; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center; }
  #video-modal .video-close { right: 12px; font-size: 22px; }
  #video-modal .video-max   { right: 56px; }
  #video-modal .video-action:hover { background: var(--cyan); transform: scale(1.08); }
  #video-modal:not(.maximized) .video-frame::after { content: ''; position: absolute; bottom: 4px; right: 4px; width: 14px; height: 14px; background: linear-gradient(135deg, transparent 0 6px, rgba(255,255,255,0.35) 6px 8px, transparent 8px 10px, rgba(255,255,255,0.35) 10px 12px, transparent 12px); pointer-events: none; }
</style>
<script>
  (function() {
    const modal = document.getElementById('video-modal');
    if (!modal) return;
    const frame = modal.querySelector('.video-frame');
    const video = modal.querySelector('.video-player');
    const title = modal.querySelector('.video-title');
    const close = modal.querySelector('.video-close');
    const max   = modal.querySelector('.video-max');
    function openVideo(src, label) {
      video.src = src;
      title.textContent = label || '';
      modal.showModal();
      video.play().catch(() => {});
    }
    function closeVideo() {
      video.pause();
      video.removeAttribute('src');
      video.load();
      modal.classList.remove('maximized');
      if (modal.open) modal.close();
    }
    function toggleMax() { modal.classList.toggle('maximized'); }
    document.querySelectorAll('a.btn-watch, a.deck-btn-watch, a.feat-card-deck-watch').forEach(a => {
      a.addEventListener('click', e => {
        if (e.metaKey || e.ctrlKey || e.shiftKey || e.button !== 0) return;
        e.preventDefault();
        const card = a.closest('.feat-card-wrap, .card, .hub-hero, .section');
        const label = card ? (card.querySelector('h1, h2, h3')?.textContent || '') : '';
        openVideo(a.getAttribute('href'), label.trim());
      });
    });
    close.addEventListener('click', closeVideo);
    max.addEventListener('click', toggleMax);
    modal.addEventListener('click', e => { if (!frame.contains(e.target)) closeVideo(); });
    modal.addEventListener('close', () => {
      video.pause(); video.removeAttribute('src'); video.load();
      modal.classList.remove('maximized');
    });
    document.addEventListener('keydown', e => {
      if (modal.open && (e.key === 'f' || e.key === 'F') && !e.target.matches('input, textarea')) toggleMax();
    });
  })();
</script>
"""


def render_module(idx: int) -> str:
    m = MODULES[idx]
    prev = MODULES[idx - 1] if idx > 0 else None
    nxt = MODULES[idx + 1] if idx < len(MODULES) - 1 else None
    body_sections = BODIES[m["slug"]]

    sections_html = []
    for eyebrow, h2, body in body_sections:
        sections_html.append(f"""
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">{eyebrow}</div>
    <h2>{h2}</h2>
    {body.strip()}
  </div>""")
    sections_block = "\n".join(sections_html)

    prev_btn = (
        f'<a class="hub-nav-btn" href="hubintl-{prev["slug"]}.html"><span class="hub-nav-label">← Previous module</span><span class="hub-nav-title">{prev["num"]} · {prev["title_word"]} {prev["title_emph"]}</span></a>'
        if prev else
        '<span class="hub-nav-btn disabled"><span class="hub-nav-label">← Previous module</span><span class="hub-nav-title">— first module —</span></span>'
    )
    next_btn = (
        f'<a class="hub-nav-btn next" href="hubintl-{nxt["slug"]}.html"><span class="hub-nav-label">Next module →</span><span class="hub-nav-title">{nxt["num"]} · {nxt["title_word"]} {nxt["title_emph"]}</span></a>'
        if nxt else
        '<span class="hub-nav-btn next disabled"><span class="hub-nav-label">Next module →</span><span class="hub-nav-title">— end of primer —</span></span>'
    )

    stats_html = "".join(
        f'<div class="hub-stat"><div class="hub-stat-value">{v}</div><div class="hub-stat-label">{l}</div></div>'
        for v, l in m["stats"]
    )

    return f"""<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>{m['num']} · {m['title_word']} {m['title_emph']} — HUB International primer</title>
<style>
{STYLE}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="hub-hero">
  <div class="hub-hero-inner">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="index.html">← ERP Unite Learning Pack</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      <a href="hubintl-primer.html">HUB International primer</a>
    </div>
    <div class="module-num">Module {m['num']} of 06</div>
    <h1>{m['title_word']} <strong>{m['title_emph']}</strong></h1>
    <p class="tagline">{m['tagline']}</p>
    <div class="hub-stats">{stats_html}</div>
    <div class="deck-link">
      <a class="deck-btn" href="hubintl-{m['slug']}-slides.html">View slides (HTML)</a>
      <a class="deck-btn deck-btn-watch" href="hubintl-{m['slug']}.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch narrated</a>
      <a class="deck-btn deck-btn-secondary" href="hubintl-{m['slug']}.pptx" download>↓ Download .pptx</a>
      <span class="deck-meta">{len(DECKS[m['slug']])} slides · HSO theme</span>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
{sections_block}

  <nav class="hub-nav">
    {prev_btn}
    <a class="hub-nav-pos" href="hubintl-primer.html">All modules · primer index</a>
    {next_btn}
  </nav>
</main>

<footer>
  Part of the <a href="index.html">ERP Unite Learning Pack</a> · also: <a href="feature-library.html">Feature library</a> · <a href="screens-library.html">Screens library</a>
</footer>
""" + VIDEO_MODAL_SNIPPET + """
</body>
</html>
"""


def render_landing() -> str:
    cards = []
    for m in MODULES:
        first_stat_value, first_stat_label = m["stats"][0]
        n_slides = len(DECKS[m['slug']])
        cards.append(f"""
    <div class="feat-card-wrap">
      <a class="feat-card" href="hubintl-{m['slug']}.html">
        <span class="num">Module {m['num']}</span>
        <h3>{m['title_word']} {m['title_emph']}</h3>
        <p>{m['tagline']}</p>
        <div class="card-stat"><span class="card-stat-value">{first_stat_value}</span><span class="card-stat-label">{first_stat_label}</span></div>
        <span class="open-cue">Open module →</span>
      </a>
      <div class="feat-card-deck-row">
        <a class="feat-card-deck" href="hubintl-{m['slug']}-slides.html">View slides ({n_slides})</a>
        <a class="feat-card-deck feat-card-deck-watch" href="hubintl-{m['slug']}.mp4" target="_blank" rel="noopener">▶ Watch</a>
        <a class="feat-card-deck feat-card-deck-pptx" href="hubintl-{m['slug']}.pptx" download>↓ .pptx</a>
      </div>
    </div>""")

    cards_block = "".join(cards)

    return f"""<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>HUB International primer — ERP Unite Learning Pack</title>
<style>
{STYLE}
/* Landing-specific */
.feat-grid {{ display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(360px, 1fr)); gap: 18px; }}
.feat-card {{ background: white; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-radius: 12px; padding: 22px 26px; text-decoration: none; color: inherit; transition: transform 0.18s ease, box-shadow 0.18s ease, border-color 0.18s ease; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 8px; min-height: 220px; }}
.feat-card:hover {{ transform: translateY(-3px); box-shadow: 0 12px 28px rgba(0, 57, 95, 0.14); border-color: var(--cyan); }}
.feat-card .num {{ font-size: 12px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--cyan); letter-spacing: 1.5px; text-transform: uppercase; }}
.feat-card h3 {{ font-size: 21px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--navy); margin: 4px 0 6px 0; line-height: 1.25; }}
.feat-card p {{ font-size: 14.5px; color: var(--slate); line-height: 1.55; }}
.feat-card .card-stat {{ display: flex; align-items: baseline; gap: 8px; margin-top: 10px; padding-top: 10px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); }}
.feat-card .card-stat-value {{ font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--cyan); }}
.feat-card .card-stat-label {{ font-size: 12px; color: var(--mute); letter-spacing: 0.5px; }}
.feat-card .open-cue {{ margin-top: auto; padding-top: 12px; color: var(--cyan); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; }}
.feat-card-wrap {{ display: flex; flex-direction: column; }}
.feat-card-deck-row {{ display: flex; margin-top: -1px; background: #F4F7FA; border: 1px solid var(--border); border-top: none; border-radius: 0 0 12px 12px; overflow: hidden; }}
.feat-card-deck {{ flex: 1; padding: 10px 18px; color: var(--slate); font-size: 13px; text-decoration: none; font-weight: 500; transition: background 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease; text-align: center; }}
.feat-card-deck:hover {{ background: var(--cyan); color: white; }}
.feat-card-deck-pptx {{ flex: 0 0 auto; border-left: 1px solid var(--border); }}
.feat-card-deck-watch {{ flex: 0 0 auto; border-left: 1px solid var(--border); color: var(--teal); font-weight: 600; }}
.feat-card-deck-watch:hover {{ background: var(--teal); color: white; }}
.features-eyebrow {{ font-size: 14px; font-weight: 700; color: var(--cyan); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 18px; padding-bottom: 10px; border-bottom: 2px solid var(--border); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: baseline; }}
.features-eyebrow .count {{ color: var(--mute); font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; }}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<header class="hub-hero">
  <div class="hub-hero-inner">
    <div class="breadcrumb">
      <a href="index.html">← ERP Unite Learning Pack</a>
      <span class="sep">/</span>
      Customer · HUB International
    </div>
    <h1>HUB <strong>International</strong> — customer primer</h1>
    <p class="tagline">Six modules that get an HSO consultant from zero to functional fluency on HUB's business, the retirement-and-wealth industry, and how that shapes the ERP Unite engagement. Source: a Hub International deep-research dossier, refracted through an HSO-implementation lens.</p>
    <div class="hub-stats">
      <div class="hub-stat"><div class="hub-stat-value">6</div><div class="hub-stat-label">modules · ~2 hrs total</div></div>
      <div class="hub-stat"><div class="hub-stat-value">$29B</div><div class="hub-stat-label">customer valuation (May 2025)</div></div>
      <div class="hub-stat"><div class="hub-stat-value">2026–27</div><div class="hub-stat-label">target IPO window</div></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</header>

<main>
  <div class="section">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Why this primer exists</div>
    <h2>HUB International is a non-trivial customer</h2>
    <p>HUB is the largest privately held insurance broker by valuation, the sixth-largest globally by revenue, and one of the two most acquisitive insurance brokers in any given year. The company has bought roughly 600 firms since 1999. The current revenue mix spans Commercial P&amp;C, Employee Benefits, Personal Insurance, and a <strong>$178B Retirement &amp; Private Wealth practice</strong> that doesn't follow insurance-brokerage economics at all.</p>
    <p>This primer is the foundation track of a larger customer pack. It exists for two reasons:</p>
    <ol>
      <li><strong>So HSO consultants don't show up under-informed.</strong> An HSO consultant who can't explain ERISA §3(38) or what a recordkeeper does cannot have a real conversation with HUB's RPW leadership. This pack closes that gap.</li>
      <li><strong>So HSO scoping calls surface the right risk question.</strong> The biggest open question in any ERP Unite engagement at HUB is whether RPW is in scope. That question only gets answered well by people who understand the practice. This primer is how we get there.</li>
    </ol>
    <p>Read the modules in order on a first pass; they build on each other. Each one ends with a five-question "Test yourself" section to confirm the material landed.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="features-eyebrow">
    <span>The six modules</span>
    <span class="count">6 modules</span>
  </div>
  <div class="feat-grid">{cards_block}
  </div>

  <div class="section" style="margin-top: 48px;">
    <div class="section-eyebrow">Coming next</div>
    <h2>Track B — ERP Unite × HUB implementation brief</h2>
    <p>The follow-on track maps each Unite hub (CashHub, CompHub, IntegrationHub, Producer Portal) through HUB's specific business shape — what statements look like with 600+ acquired entities, where the RPW gap actually lives in the data model, and which carriers and recordkeepers we need day-1 feeds from. Pending commit.</p>
  </div>
</main>

<footer>
  Part of the <a href="index.html">ERP Unite Learning Pack</a> · also: <a href="feature-library.html">Feature library</a> · <a href="screens-library.html">Screens library</a> · Source: <a href="source-docs/hub-international-dossier.md">HUB International dossier</a>
</footer>
""" + VIDEO_MODAL_SNIPPET + """
</body>
</html>
"""


def main() -> None:
    # Modules — HTML
    for i, m in enumerate(MODULES):
        out = OUTPUT_DIR / f"hubintl-{m['slug']}.html"
        out.write_text(render_module(i), encoding="utf-8")
        print(f"  wrote {out.name}  ({len(BODIES[m['slug']])} sections)")

    # Modules — Marp markdown source for slide decks
    for i, m in enumerate(MODULES):
        out = OUTPUT_DIR / f"hubintl-{m['slug']}.md"
        out.write_text(render_deck(i), encoding="utf-8")
        print(f"  wrote {out.name}  ({len(DECKS[m['slug']])} slides)")

    # Landing
    landing = OUTPUT_DIR / "hubintl-primer.html"
    landing.write_text(render_landing(), encoding="utf-8")
    print(f"  wrote {landing.name}  (primer landing)")


if __name__ == "__main__":
    main()
